From 7b46b249b04a0ea6a3113f3634f620955ed8a2fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@collabora.com>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 13:43:41 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: mediatek: Allow trigger-sources on
 relevant HW

Most of the MediaTek Display Controller hardware sub-IPs need a
specific (and reserved to them) MuteX trigger.

Since now MuteX is a trigger source, allow specifying trigger
sources in all of the display IPs that support one.

Reviewed-by: Krzysztof Kozlowski <krzysztof.kozlowski@oss.qualcomm.com>
Signed-off-by: AngeloGioacchino Del Regno <angelogioacchino.delregno@collabora.com>
Link: https://patchwork.kernel.org/project/linux-mediatek/list/?series=1127365
[dianqk: from the Huge Restructuring v2 series, applied to v7.3-rc6; rc6 drift resolved]
